.TH MD_RESET 3 "2026-10-16" "libmorsedec 0.3.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
md_reset \- clear a stream while retaining its configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <morsedec.h>

int md_reset(morsedec_decoder_t *decoder);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Clear a stream while retaining its configuration.
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I decoder
Decoder handle. Calls using this handle must be serialized, including queries.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns MORSEDEC_SUCCESS (1) on success, or MORSEDEC_FAILURE (0) and sets
errno on failure. Do not inspect errno after success.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
decoder is NULL.
.SH REMARKS
Discards buffered input, channels, pins, messages, learned duration statistics
and the sample/spectrum input-mode selection. Resets frame count to zero. The
audio versus I/Q handle type, geometry, FFT plan and preallocated storage are
preserved. Channel IDs from the discarded stream become invalid and are not
reused on subsequent streams of this handle. Borrowed views are invalidated.
Use this after md_flush(), before switching input mode, or after a
discontinuity. Reset performs no heap allocation and does not flush discarded
output.
.PP
Preserves the worker pool and its thread budget; creates no new workers.
.SH THREAD SAFETY
Serialize all calls that access the same handle, including getters. Different
handles may process concurrently after construction. These functions are not
specified as async-signal-safe.
.SH VERSION
This md_ entry point is available since libmorsedec 0.2.0.
Version 0.3.0 uses the float API and shared-library ABI 2.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmorsedec (3),
.BR md_flush (3),
.BR md_get_geometry (3),
.BR md_get_channel (3)
